  <article class="post-content">
    <h1>Ruqya. Islam. The Unseen.</h1>

    <p>
      This blog is about what Islam teaches regarding Ruqya, the unseen, jinn, sihr, the evil
      eye, protection, and spiritual life.
    </p>

    <p>
      There is a lot of information about these subjects. Much of it is mixed with culture,
      personal stories, exaggeration, and claims with no evidence.
    </p>

    <p>We separate them.</p>

    <p>The standard is simple:</p>

    <p><strong>Quran. Authentic Sunnah. Evidence.</strong></p>

    <p>If something is established, we say so.</p>
    <p>If something is uncertain, we say so.</p>
    <p>If something is simply folklore, we call it folklore.</p>

    <p>
      We do not invent stories about the unseen. We do not promise miracles. We do not turn fear
      into business.
    </p>

    <p>
      Ruqya is not magic. The unseen is not entertainment. And unexplained events are not
      automatically caused by jinn.
    </p>

    <p>At the same time, we do not reject what Islam clearly teaches simply because we cannot see it.</p>

    <p><strong>Believe what is true. Question what is uncertain. Reject what has no basis.</strong></p>

    <p>That is the purpose of this blog.</p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Spotted an error, or have a topic you'd like covered? Visit the <a href="/contact">contact
      page</a> to get in touch.
    </p>
  </article>
